#NEXUS

[ martínez2009b_fig10: Early dinosaur summary tree. Dinosauria, Ornithischia, Saurischia, Theropoda and Sauropodomorpha, joined by arrows to red node dots, are kept as internal labels. Two dots sit on a vertical shared with the node below: Ornithischia's dot is where the (Pisanosaurus, other Ornithischia) line leaves the Dinosauria vertical, below Silesaurus, and Theropoda's where Neotheropoda leaves, above the entering stem; each dot is read as its own node, so (Silesaurus, (Pisanosaurus, other Ornithischia)) and (Guaibasaurus, Neotheropoda) are clades. Fully resolved. 12 tips, fully resolved; 5 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Random-sample case (seed 20261114). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=12;
    TAXLABELS
        Outgroup
        Silesaurus
        Pisanosaurus
        other_Ornithischia
        Herrerasaurus
        Staurikosaurus
        Eoraptor
        Guaibasaurus
        Neotheropoda
        Panphagia
        Saturnalia
        other_Sauropodomorpha
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE 'martínez2009b_fig10' = [&R] (Outgroup,((Silesaurus,(Pisanosaurus,other_Ornithischia))Ornithischia,((Herrerasaurus,Staurikosaurus),(Eoraptor,((Guaibasaurus,Neotheropoda)Theropoda,(Panphagia,(Saturnalia,other_Sauropodomorpha))Sauropodomorpha)))Saurischia)Dinosauria);
END;
